openSUSE Build Service publishing
=================================

This package is published via the openSUSE Build Service in the
project home:mjgajda, which rebuilds it for Debian and Ubuntu
targets from source.

Package-specific configuration
------------------------------

The canonical OBS source-service definition is in
debian/obs/_service.  It tells OBS to fetch this git repository's
debian/latest branch and assemble a source package.  The _service
file in the repo is the single source of truth; the copy held by
OBS is kept in sync from it.

Target distributions built by OBS:

  - Debian 13 (trixie)
  - Debian unstable
  - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble)

Adding or removing a target is an edit to the project metadata
on OBS and, for the apt-repo channel, a matching change in
debian/reprepro/conf/distributions.

Syncing the repo to OBS
-----------------------

    debian/scripts/publish.sh            show drift between the
                                         repo and OBS
    debian/scripts/publish.sh --push     sync debian/obs/_service
                                         into OBS and trigger a build
    debian/scripts/publish.sh --pull     overwrite the local
                                         _service from OBS
